(Bug #50: LANGUAGE.md documents a bare `otherwise` clause on a `but if`
 chain over any base action, but the chain-continuation guard only accepted
 `but`, a comma and `and`, so `otherwise` after a `print` base was a parse
 error - "Expected a statement, got Otherwise". The `but otherwise`
 spelling always worked; both must, and both must pick the same branch.)

a number called gauge is 8.
print gauge, but if gauge is greater than 50 print "high", otherwise print "low".
print gauge, but if gauge is greater than 50 print "high", but otherwise print "low".
print gauge, but if gauge is greater than 5 print "high", otherwise print "low".
